      "evidence": "Picks and who-it-is-not-for are present, but the SavorOne recommendation threshold ('roughly $1,300 a year in bonus-category spending just to break even') is arithmetically wrong. Break-even versus a flat 2% card is category spend B = 0.5 x total spend + fee/0.02, i.e. half of total spending plus $1,950 a year, matching the page's own later 55 to 60 percent figure."
